# OpenGamepadUI — the gamepad shell gamescope hosts. Local PKGBUILD (packages/opengamepadui/PKGBUILD).
#
# Was a prebuilt pin of upstream's aarch64 release tarball until 2026-10-02, when the first hardware
# boot (KONKR Pocket FIT, SM8650) showed v0.46.1 needs the first two patches below on these boards:
#
#   0001  upstream #542: HardwareManager reads /sys/devices/virtual/dmi/id/product_name, which does
#         not exist on a devicetree board (no SMBIOS from the ABL UEFI), and calls a method on the
#         null FileAccess -- a SIGSEGV in a release build, ~10s into every start, so the session
#         crash-loops behind a black panel. On ARM the name comes from the devicetree model
#         instead ("Unknown" if empty), as asked in review of upstream PR #559.
#   0002  upstream #540: Godot 4.7 added a native Control.custom_maximum_size, so the two install
#         dialogs that declare their own fail to compile, and game_launch_menu.gd (which depends on
#         them) never loads -- picking a game does nothing, on every platform.
#   0003  ours, for upstream: the performance menu showed TDP, thermal-limit and power-profile
#         controls for any integrated GPU. An SoC GPU (Adreno, via our PowerStation devfreq
#         backend) has none of them, so they appeared with a -1 range and wrote nowhere. Shown now
#         only when HardwareManager reports the capability.
#   0004  ours, for upstream: an app that exits before creating a window never left the running
#         list (its type stays unknown, and only X11/Wayland apps get the is_running() checks), so
#         a ROM whose emulator is not installed hung on the loading screen and the plugin's EXIT
#         hook never ran. While the type is unknown, mark the app stopped on the first failed
#         is_running() check (the reaper it tracks outlives every process of the app), ~1 s.
#   0005  ours, for upstream (to confirm with the authors first): a missing default performance
#         profile is created from the settings applied at that moment, which on a fresh install
#         is when the last game stops -- a game's CPU core count became the default and stayed
#         applied after it exited (HW, Pocket FIT, 2026-10-04). Save the startup settings as the
#         default of each profile state (docked = charging, undocked) that has none.
#   0006  ours, for upstream (branch feat/power-profiles-without-tdp): power profiles on a GPU
#         with no TDP. PowerStation's devfreq backend offers them (CPU + GPU governor pairs), but
#         the menu only showed the dropdown for a matched AMD APU, only in simple mode, and as
#         presets that also reset cores / GPU clocks; a mode toggle forced max-performance. For
#         a GPU without a TDP: dropdown in both modes, a choice applies alone, toggles keep it.
#         The dropdown sits above the Advanced Mode toggle (a profile sets CPU + GPU governors).
#   0007  ours, for upstream (branch fix/profile-key-app-id): a game's performance profile was saved
#         under a hash of its card NAME, so renaming a card lost it (RetroForge renames same-named ROM
#         cards, and a metadata scrape will rename them all). Keyed by provider + app id now (for
#         RetroForge ROMs, <system>/<file>); a profile saved under the name is still loaded.
#   0008  ours, for upstream: the home banner's god-rays shader (screen texture with mipmaps,
#         animated with TIME) and the focused card's god-rays + shine keep the whole UI redrawing
#         every frame, so low_processor_mode never idles: measured 47 ms of GPU per frame, the
#         Adreno 610 pinned at 1050 MHz and the shell at ~20 fps doing nothing (Air X, 2026-10-10;
#         hiding that one node took the shell to zero submits and the GPU to runtime-suspend).
#         A Settings > General "Animated Effects" toggle (general/animated_effects), off by
#         default, gates those shaders.
#   0009  ours, for upstream: the home banner's tile collage was clipped with clip_children (an
#         offscreen canvas group + mask every frame) by an all-opaque gradient, i.e. a plain
#         rectangle. clip_contents (a scissor) gives the same picture: 19.6 -> 13.9 ms of GPU per
#         frame on the Adreno 610 at 1920x1080 (Air X, 2026-10-10).
#   0010  ours, for upstream: InputPlumberInstance emits its signals (input_event through its
#         DBusDevices, composite_device_added, started) from inside process() while bound, so a
#         handler calling back into it panics in godot-rust and gets nil. Pressing A on Gamepad
#         Settings made is_running() fail ("InputPlumber service not available"), and the icon
#         processor's get_composite_device() failed on every gamepad action (empty device name,
#         default icons). 130+ panics a session (Air Y, 2026-10-11). Handlers connected deferred.
#   0011  ours, for upstream: SettingsManager.get_value without a default logged a ConfigFile
#         error per unset key (six per game in the launch settings), erase on an unset key
#         another; the plugin store menu took the offline null as a Dictionary and errored.
#   0012  ours, for upstream: MANGMI pads matched no icon mapping (a warning per icon refresh);
#         the Xbox Series mapping takes "MANGMI". Digital L2/R2 (Gamepad:Button:*Trigger) get the
#         trigger icons, and Gamepad Settings stops warning about the Sync capability.
#   0013  ours, for upstream: one GPU needs no glxinfo to be found active (absent on SoC boards:
#         "Failed to run glxinfo" + "Could not identify active GPU" on every query).
#   0014  ours, for upstream: the home screen warned for each recent app no library provides
#         (an emulator started on its own, Steam, a ROM before its plugin library loads) on every
#         refresh; the icon processor flipped the device name to "" on OGUI's own actions.
#   0015  ours, for upstream: the main menu's running-game card showed "Game Name" for an app no
#         library provides (an emulator opened from RetroForge's Emulators page): it returned early
#         when the library lookup missed, also skipping its window buttons. Falls back to the launch
#         item's name, as the quick bar does (HW, Pocket ACE, 2026-10-17).
#   0016  ours, for upstream: nothing starts the shared ThreadPool (thread_pool.tres) any more, so the
#         Steam plugin's library refresh after login queued forever and the Steam library never
#         loaded (HW, Pocket ACE, 2026-10-17). exec() starts the pool on first use; the resource's
#         `size = null` is dropped.
#   0017  ours, for upstream: a Steam launch ended (the client SIGTERMed) once only Steam windows were
#         left for 4 s, which a first Proton launch always reaches (driver query, prefix setup, windowless install
#         scripts: DirectX, PhysX, EOS). A launch now counts as alive while Steam's own
#         "reaper SteamLaunch" runs (HW, Pocket ACE, 2026-10-17, Trine on Proton 11 arm64). The
#         reaper's /proc/<pid>/cmdline is read past its first NUL: get_string_from_utf8() stops
#         there in Godot 4.7.1, so only argv[0] came out and no reaper matched (HW, KONKR Pocket
#         FIT, 2026-10-19; was a separate 0020).
#   0018  ours, for upstream: joining Wi-Fi from Settings > Network saved a password one character
#         too long and the UI had no way to undo it (HW, Air X, 2026-10-18). NetworkManager stored
#         exactly what the dialog held, and the dialog never cleared its field: a mistyped password
#         stayed behind the dots and went out again on every retry. Every join also added a profile
#         beside the saved ones (a corrected password sat next to the wrong one; a failed join stayed
#         for NetworkManager to retry), networks could not be forgotten, "Connected" showed for an
#         access point still being tried, and a dialog left unsubmitted kept its submit handler (the
#         next Submit joined that network too). Now: a fresh hidden field per dialog with Show
#         password, B closes it, Forget network (all its profiles, via nmcli), a join that follows
#         its own activation and keeps one profile (the new one once it works, else the old ones),
#         Connected only when activated, and a new core instance once the old one loses the Wi-Fi
#         device (after a NetworkManager restart it knew only the P2P device, so joins had no
#         effect). First boot: same field/submit fixes.
#   0019  ours, for upstream: a launched app's new windows switched the gamescope baselayer to the
#         first new one, and the ids come sorted: Steam's Big Picture window arrived with helper
#         windows of lower id that never become focusable, one of those got the focus and was then
#         dropped as not focusable, and nothing switched to Big Picture -- a black screen over a running
#         Steam (HW, KONKR Pocket FIT, 2026-10-19). Now a focusable new window is preferred, and
#         with none focused, a running app's window that becomes focusable gets the focus, deferred
#         out of gamescope's signal (switch_window calls back into GamescopeInstance, which
#         godot-rust refuses while it is bound). When the focused window goes (a launcher's
#         short-lived startup window), the app's newest focusable window gets the focus, from
#         either handler; it is removed only when there is none (issue #29: loading screen over a
#         running Steam, KONKR Pocket FIT, 2026-11-01; was a separate 0044).
#   0021  ours, for upstream: OGUI's desktop library lists the shortcut Steam writes for each game it
#         installs, and its quirk for them added '-silent' only (the Steam plugin's flags are there,
#         commented out). Without -gamepadui Steam came up in its desktop mode over the game: a
#         sign-in window, the desktop library and a "Launching..." dialog (HW, KONKR Pocket FIT,
#         2026-10-21). The quirk now adds the Steam plugin's flags.
#   0022  ours, for upstream: LaunchManager warned about every orphan window (one no running app
#         claims) on every check_running(), once a second. Steam kept running between games has a
#         dozen such windows, so the journal took two lines a second idle in the menu and ~4.5
#         during a game (HW, KONKR Pocket FIT, 2026-10-22). Warned once per change of the set now.
#   0023  ours, for upstream: the home screen reused a recent app's card by name, so a game a library
#         dropped and added again kept a card on the old LibraryItem, which has no launch item: its
#         page showed no art and Play did nothing (HW, KONKR Pocket FIT, 2026-10-22: Hades, first
#         listed by Steam's desktop shortcut, which the RetroForge plugin removes). A card frees
#         itself on removed_from_library, but only listens once its art has loaded. Reused now only
#         while it shows the very item.
#   0024  ours, agreed with ShadowApex 2026-10-26: no InputPlumber intercept mode. OGUI loads
#         ogui_focus.json (every input -> its DBus UI action) while it has focus, and in game the
#         game's profile: OGUI's per-game setting, else the one the launcher declares in
#         $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/opengamepadui/game_profile (retroforge-launch, "gamepad_profile"), else
#         the global one. A JSON game profile gets Guide -> [layer, ui_guide] and the layer gets
#         Guide+A -> ui_quick, Guide+X -> ui_osk where it leaves them free (our YAML profiles carry
#         them, test-launch checks); a Guide release without its press is ignored (a combo that
#         opened a menu swapped the profile while Guide was held). The single-cap [Guide] intercept flipped to
#         Always on the Guide press and ate the emulator hotkey layer (HW, MANGMI Air X,
#         2026-10-21). Also fixes set_gamepad_profile() never loading on a device with a gamepad
#         target (it broke out of the device loop first). Whole numbers in the edited JSON are
#         written back as integers: Godot read `version` as 1.0 and InputPlumber refused the file,
#         so a game with no profile of its own kept the focus profile and got no input (HW, MANGMI
#         Pocket Max, 2026-10-27: PortMaster). Goes with inputplumber patch 0002.
#   0025  ours, for upstream: a game started from the Steam client's own UI, with the client launched by
#         OGUI as an app of its own (Main menu > Emulators > Steam Client), got the client's app id:
#         RunningApp stamps STEAM_GAME on every window of the app, every check, and the game runs under
#         the client. gamescope reported the client focused and Steam gave the game no Steam Input (HW,
#         MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-23: SuperTux, no controller). A window whose process has SteamGameId
#         keeps that id now, goes ahead of the app's in the baselayer app ids while focused, and
#         LaunchManager maps it to the app. Same ids as before for steam://rungameid, clientless and
#         every other launch.
#   0026  ours, for upstream: card_ui.tscn's MarginContainer sizes the on-screen keyboard to the whole
#         screen, and its root passed mouse events, so while it was up it took every touch above the menu:
#         a dialog's Submit over the keyboard could not be tapped (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-23: Settings
#         > Network's Wi-Fi password). The root ignores mouse events now; the keys and their panel still
#         take theirs. "opened" only when it was closed, a second open() only retargets: once taps
#         reached the menu, a tap on the field opened it again and the SpacerGrowerEffect pushed
#         the menu up by another keyboard height per tap (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-23; was a
#         separate 0028).
#   0027  ours, for upstream: Wi-Fi rows were keyed by SSID but made per access point, so a network with
#         two radios or mesh nodes showed twice, and showing Settings > Network started two refreshes at
#         once that each made rows (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-23). One row per network, for its strongest
#         access point, which a join takes too; one refresh at a time, none while hidden.
#   0029  ours, for upstream: Forget network (0018) is in the password dialog, which only secured networks
#         opened, so the open network in use could not be forgotten (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-23). That
#         network opens it too, without the password field and Submit: only Forget network. The
#         first-boot screen, which shares the network list and has no Forget, ignores that network
#         instead of showing it a password dialog.
#   0030  ours, for upstream: CardButton emitted "pressed" when a click or tap went down, so Submit closed
#         the Wi-Fi dialog under the finger and the release landed on the row behind it (HW, MANGMI Air
#         X, 2026-10-24). "pressed" on release over the button, as Godot's buttons; button_down unchanged.
#   0031  ours, for upstream: AudioManager.set_volume() sets the level only, and WirePlumber restores a
#         sink's saved mute at every boot, so a muted speaker stayed silent while the slider and keys
#         moved the level (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-24). A volume above zero now also unmutes the sink.
#   0032  ours, for upstream: every card loaded its art when built, and each library tab builds a card
#         per item, so a library's whole art stayed in GPU memory: 872 MiB in the idle shell with 1,000
#         games (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-24). A card in a ScrollContainer now loads it within a screen
#         of the visible part and drops it past three or 10 s after the container hides
#         (CardArtWindow): 310 MiB. A card not in the tree yet still costs its caller a frame, so the
#         library menu's refreshes keep merging (without it, a 33 s freeze at that size). A tab built
#         hidden counts once laid out while visible: until then its cards all sit at 0, and its first
#         show loaded all 1,000. Switching tabs then peaks at 359 MiB instead of 937.
#   0033  ours, for upstream: launcher.json's "recent" list held a null, saved by Play on a home card
#         left on a replaced library item (0023), and every reader got a null for a name (the home
#         screen reads each into a String: a script error). get_recent_apps() returns names only, and
#         saving the list drops the rest (HW, KONKR Pocket FIT, 2026-10-22).
#   0034  ours, for upstream with 0017: through the client, Steam's install scripts run in Proton, whose
#         hidden windows set the game running; once they were gone Steam was stopped at its "Processing
#         Vulkan shaders" prompt, before it started the game (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-24). A launch
#         counts once Steam's reaper for the game itself has run (not its "Install=1" one).
#   0035  ours, for upstream with 0023: the library tabs kept a card per name, left on a replaced
#         LibraryItem with no launch item (placeholder art, nothing to Play) when a library dropped a
#         game and added it again (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-24: Hades, once the plugin dropped Steam's
#         desktop shortcut). A card is reused only while it shows the very item.
#   0036  ours, for upstream: each card masked its art to its rounded corners with clip_children (a
#         canvas group, an offscreen pass per card every frame), and its shadow filled the card behind
#         the art twice. Library > All Games, 18 cards, Adreno 610 (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-24):
#         3.2 + 2.1 of 14.4 ms of GPU per frame under Vulkan; under OpenGL each group also flushes the
#         frame, and the page drew at 31 fps with the GPU 42% busy. The art rounds its own corners in
#         a shader now, the panel masks only while a progress bar or focus effect is over the art, and
#         the shadow draws its ring only: 59 fps under OpenGL.
#   0037  ours, for upstream: 164 Buttons with an empty _process, the context bar's hidden debug label
#         rebuilt every frame, and 19 ScrollerJoysticks polling a centred stick: the idle shell's main
#         thread 12% -> 9.5% of a core (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-24).
#   0038  ours, for upstream: home and the library skip scrolling to the focused card while
#         InputManager.current_touches > 0 or the left button is down. A touch release that never
#         reached InputManager left the count above zero, and the library no longer followed the D-pad
#         (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-25). They now skip it only within 500 ms of the last touch, drag
#         or mouse button (InputManager.pointer_recent).
#   0039  ours, RetroForge-only: no plugin store and no plugin manager. RetroForge ships its one plugin
#         in the image and updates it by OTA; the store offered plugins that cannot work here (the
#         Steam plugin's sign-in runs steamcmd, x86), and the Plugins page could disable ours. The
#         two Settings buttons go (their menus stay, tabs are set by index, but fetch and poll
#         nothing), and the first boot's plugin step skips itself (user, 2026-10-29).
#   0040  ours, for upstream: HardwareManager read all ~42,000 lines of pci.ids for a platform GPU
#         (no PCI vendor id, and "" prefixes every line: 0.6 s before the first frame, MANGMI Air
#         X), ran vulkaninfo only to match PCI ids such a card has none of, and read every sysfs
#         attribute with a `cat` process. A card without a vendor id skips the lookup, vulkaninfo
#         runs only when a card has PCI ids, attributes are read directly.
#   0041  ours, for upstream: InputIconManager loaded all sixteen icon mappings, with their
#         textures, three times while it was created, and each icon lookup loaded the device's
#         mapping again (~3,000 of the 3,600 resources loaded at startup, MANGMI Air X). One pass
#         collects both maps, and the mappings in use are held.
#   0042  ours, for upstream: the Disks settings menu built a card per partition (~85 on a
#         handheld's internal storage) as the card UI loaded and again when udisks2 settled: ~2 s
#         on the main thread before the first frame (MANGMI Air X). Built when the menu is shown;
#         a change while hidden only marks them out of date.
#   0043  ours, for upstream: focused_app_updated's handler (current app, app_switched, gamepad
#         profile) ran inside GamescopeInstance.process(), and what it calls goes back into the
#         instance (get_xwayland): godot-rust refuses that, and OpenGamepadUI died of SIGSEGV
#         when the store sign-in's Chromium window was adopted while the kept Steam client ran
#         (KONKR Pocket FIT, 2026-11-01, issue #28). The handler now only queues the change.
#   0045  ours, for upstream: the volume keys moved the volume by 6%, and left/right moved the quick
#         settings volume slider by 1 and the brightness slider by 3 (user, 2026-11-08). All move by 5
#         now; a slider snaps to its step, so a volume left off the grid lands on a multiple of 5.
#         The Saturation slider is hidden: its handler does nothing upstream ("TODO: Deprecate").
#   0046  ours, for upstream: Settings > General showed "Unknown" for BIOS Version and an empty Vendor
#         on every Arm board (no DMI on a devicetree board) and the core types for CPU Model
#         (lscpu's model names on Arm, "Cortex-A510 Cortex-A715 ..."). CPU Model is now the SoC's
#         name from Qualcomm socinfo (by soc0/soc_id, e.g. 603 "Qualcomm Dragonwing QCS8550";
#         unlisted ids "Qualcomm <machine>"), the BIOS and Vendor rows hide when empty, and a Memory
#         row shows MemTotal rounded to the capacity sold (8, 12, 16 GB...); Kernel Version drops
#         uname's trailing newline, which made its row two lines tall (user, 2026-11-09).
#   0047  ours, for upstream: the volume sliders showed 0 at startup while the speaker played. The
#         volume is read once, asynchronously, from AudioManager._init(): the menus are built before
#         it arrives and nothing tells them, and before WirePlumber has a default sink the read fails
#         (-1) and is never retried; the volume keys stepped from that 0 too. It is now retried once a
#         second for up to 30 s and announced with volume_read, which the menus show without writing
#         it back (that would clear a mute, 0031; the 5-step slider of 0045 snaps it on screen only)
#         and without the volume indicator (user, 2026-11-05).
#   0048  ours, for upstream: the screen dimmed after the inactivity timeout while a game was being
#         played. PowerSaver restarted its timers from _input(), but InputManager (a later sibling, so
#         its _input() runs first) marks every Godot joypad event handled while InputPlumber runs. The
#         menu's input comes over DBus and got through; a game's comes only as those joypad events
#         (its profile drives the virtual controller), so none reached PowerSaver. It now watches the
#         window's window_input signal, emitted before any node handles the event; a stick resting
#         below 0.2 is not activity (user, 2026-11-09).
#   0049  ours, for upstream: a secured network's password dialog, on the first-boot network screen
#         and in Settings > Network, opened with no on-screen keyboard (only A on the field opened
#         it). It opens with the dialog now (not for the open network in use), and Enter on the
#         keyboard submits the password in both. On first boot Enter only closed the keyboard and
#         gave the focus back to the field, whose unset D-pad neighbours let the network list behind
#         the dialog take it; the neighbours stay in the dialog now (as 0018 did for Settings >
#         Network), and after a submit the focus goes to Next, not back to the list (user,
#         2026-11-10). Settings' Enter submitted before the keyboard's refocus of the field, which
#         could leave the focus on the hidden field: both submit deferred now. A tapped Submit on
#         first boot closes a keyboard still up (user, 2026-11-09).
#   0050  ours, for upstream: at a larger UI scale the Settings category list on the left outgrows the
#         screen, and the D-pad took the focus below it without scrolling: the scroll bar had to be
#         dragged (user, 2026-11-11). follow_focus on that list and on a game's settings list, built the
#         same way, and on the Display, Network, Bluetooth and Disks pages (General, Library and
#         Plugins already had it).
#   0051  ours, for upstream: in Settings and a game's settings the D-pad could not move between the
#         category list and its page: Right on a category did nothing (only A opened it, e.g. Display
#         > Scale) and Left on a page did nothing (only B), as each column's FocusGroup points Left and
#         Right at the control itself (user, 2026-11-11). Right on a category opens its page, as A
#         does; Left on a page goes back, as B does, where Left has nothing to do there (not on a
#         slider, a text field, a list or tab bar that uses Left, a row with a left neighbour, or a
#         dialog), and only from the page itself, not a level it opened.
#
# 0020, 0028 and 0044 fixed the patch they follow and were folded into it (0017, 0026, 0019) on
# 2026-11-11; their numbers stay unused so the others keep theirs.
#
# The earlier 0006/0007 (plugin store URL as a project setting, set to "" for RetroForge) were dropped on
# 2026-10-06: with the store off, OGUI's first-start screen showed an empty catalog. 0039 removes the
# store for good, that screen included (it now skips itself).
#
# So the PKGBUILD keeps upstream's aarch64 engine binary, Rust core and reaper from the release
# tarball, and rebuilds only opengamepad-ui.pck from the tagged source plus these patches. Drop a
# patch when the release that fixes it is pinned.
#
# Fields (see packages/README.md):
#   name           pkgname (must match the PKGBUILD); also the work/ build-dir + repo entry
#   pkgbuild_local path (relative to this dir) to the checked-in PKGBUILD to build
#   pkgrel_suffix  numeric suffix appended to the PKGBUILD's pkgrel so pacman prefers our build
#   patches        files under patches/, applied in order right after prepare()'s first `cd`
name: opengamepadui
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
pkgrel_suffix: 1
